IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cr2-nouns`
IMPORT `cr2-seat`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- WORKED CASES OF THE SEAT LAYER (layer 2).
-- One case at least for every question of cr2-seat.l4, told in the facts a person in the seat would state.
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the regulation and counting on a calendar before the rules were run.
-- Abbreviations for the items of the lists, so that a case reads on one line:

§ `Worked cases -- the questions of a person who contributes to or may claim from the Plan`

`seat item 46(2)(a)` MEANS `reg 46(2)(a) — the dates of marriage and dissolution of marriage of the persons subject to the division`
`seat item 46(2)(b)` MEANS `reg 46(2)(b) — the period of cohabitation for which the division has been made`
`seat item 46(2)(c)` MEANS `reg 46(2)(c) — the unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons before the division`
`seat item 52(a)(i)` MEANS `reg 52(a)(i) — the name at birth, present name, sex, address and Social Insurance Number of the applicant or beneficiary`
`seat item 52(b)(i)` MEANS `reg 52(b)(i) — the date and place of birth of the applicant or beneficiary`
`seat item 52(c)` MEANS `reg 52(c) — the date and place of death of the contributor`
`seat item 53(a)` MEANS `reg 53(a) — the name and date of birth of all children for whom the contributor received family allowance benefits or Canada child benefits`
`seat item 53(c)` MEANS `reg 53(c) — the periods during which the contributor received those benefits for those children`
`seat item 54(1) chapeau` MEANS `reg 54(1) chapeau — the information required under regulation 52, with any modifications that the circumstances require`
`seat item 54(1)(d)` MEANS `reg 54(1)(d) — the date and place of marriage and the certificate of marriage, a copy of it or a copy of the act of marriage`
`seat item 54(2)(a)` MEANS `reg 54(2)(a) — the name at birth, present name, sex, address and Social Insurance Number of each of the former spouses`
`seat item 54(2)(i)` MEANS `reg 54(2)(i) — a copy of any written agreement between the persons subject to a division that was made before June 4, 1986, or on or after that date and binds the Minister under subsection 55.2(3) of the Act`
`seat item 54.1(1)(e)` MEANS `reg 54.1(1)(e) — the month in which the spouses or common-law partners commenced to live together in a conjugal relationship`
`seat item 54.1(1)(g)` MEANS `reg 54.1(1)(g) — documentary evidence of the dissolution of any previous marriage of the applicant`

§§ `Cases -- interpretation (regulation 37)`

-- Case: Priya received a Canada child benefit notice for her 5-year-old (the deemed overpayment under section 122.61).
#ASSERT `Is this payment a Canada child benefit (reg 37(1))` TRUE TRUE
-- Her cousin's payment is for a child of eight: not within "qualified dependant under seven".
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this payment a Canada child benefit (reg 37(1))` TRUE FALSE)
-- Case: Omar's father died leaving an estate; Omar is the executor.
#ASSERT `Am I the personal representative of a deceased person (reg 37(1))` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Case: Leila's husband died with no estate; she is the survivor.
#ASSERT `Am I the personal representative of a deceased person (reg 37(1))` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Case: with no estate and no survivor, the next of kin is the personal representative.
#ASSERT `Am I the personal representative of a deceased person (reg 37(1))` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Case: there is an estate, and the survivor is neither executor, administrator, heir nor in control: not the personal representative.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I the personal representative of a deceased person (reg 37(1))` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Case: an agency designated to receive a deceased beneficiary's unpaid payment, to which section 60(2) did not already apply.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make an application (reg 37(2))` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to make an application (reg 37(2))` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to receive benefits (reg 37(3))` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to receive benefits (reg 37(3))` FALSE FALSE)
-- Case: Darius, a student hired on a casual basis by a federal department.
#ASSERT `Am I a prescribed individual for the definition public officer (reg 37(4))` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a prescribed individual for the definition public officer (reg 37(4))` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Cases -- the Record of Earnings (regulations 39 to 41)`

-- Case: Mei applies in writing with her name, address with postal code and Social Insurance Number.
#ASSERT `Is my application for a statement of my earnings made as the Regulations require (reg 39)` `an application in writing to the Minister` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Case: Noah applies on the Internet form with name, Social Insurance Number and postal code.
#ASSERT `Is my application for a statement of my earnings made as the Regulations require (reg 39)` `an application to the Minister by way of the Internet on the electronic form prescribed for that purpose` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Case: an application made by telephone is not one the Regulations provide for.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my application for a statement of my earnings made as the Regulations require (reg 39)` `an application made in some other way` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Case: a reduction in Mei's Record of Earnings that section 97(4) requires her to be told about.
#ASSERT `Must the Minister notify me in writing of a reduction in my Record of Earnings (reg 40)` TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the notice of a reduction in my Record of Earnings in the form required (reg 40)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the notice of a reduction in my Record of Earnings in the form required (reg 40)` TRUE FALSE)
-- Case: Jean worked in Quebec in 2019; the plan took 2,700 of base contributions at 5.4 per cent: 2,700 x 100 / 2.7 = 100,000.
#ASSERT `What are the salary and wages on which a contribution has been made for me under a provincial pension plan (reg 41)` `the base tier` 2019 2700 5.4 EQUALS JUST 100000
-- First additional contributions of 500 at 1 per cent (2019): 500 x 100 / 0.5 = 100,000.
#ASSERT `What are the salary and wages on which a contribution has been made for me under a provincial pension plan (reg 41)` `the first additional tier` 2019 500 1 EQUALS JUST 100000
-- Second additional contributions of 300 at 4 per cent in 2024: 300 x 100 / 2 = 15,000. Before 2024 the text gives nothing.
#ASSERT `What are the salary and wages on which a contribution has been made for me under a provincial pension plan (reg 41)` `the second additional tier` 2024 300 4 EQUALS JUST 15000
#ASSERT `What are the salary and wages on which a contribution has been made for me under a provincial pension plan (reg 41)` `the second additional tier` 2023 300 4 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Cases -- recovery of an overpayment (regulation 42)`

-- Case: Sam owes a 300 overpayment and is owed a 500 benefit; 100 is to be deducted; no hardship.
#ASSERT `Can an overpayment I owe be deducted from a benefit payable to me or my estate (reg 42)` TRUE TRUE 100 500 300 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can an overpayment I owe be deducted from a benefit payable to me or my estate (reg 42)` TRUE TRUE 100 500 300 TRUE)

§§ `Cases -- applications (regulations 43 to 46.1)`

#ASSERT `Is my application made as the Regulations require (reg 43(1))` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my application made as the Regulations require (reg 43(1))` FALSE)
-- Case: Rosa, born 1 March 1962, applied for a disability pension on 1 January 2022; denied 1 June 2022, notified 10 June 2022;
-- she asks in writing on 28 September 2022 (the last day: 30 June + 90 days) that it be treated as a retirement pension application.
#ASSERT `Is my denied application for a disability pension deemed to be an application for a retirement pension (reg 43(1.1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1962 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 6 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 9 28) (YearMonthDay 2022 6 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1)
-- One day later she is out of time.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my denied application for a disability pension deemed to be an application for a retirement pension (reg 43(1.1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1962 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 6 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 9 29) (YearMonthDay 2022 6 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1))
-- If the denial was confirmed on appeal and she was told on 15 November 2022, she has until 13 February 2023.
#ASSERT `Is my denied application for a disability pension deemed to be an application for a retirement pension (reg 43(1.1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1962 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 6 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 2 13) (YearMonthDay 2022 6 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 11 15)
#ASSERT `What is the last day for my request (reg 43(1.1)(b))` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 6 29)
#ASSERT `What is the last day for my request (reg 43(1.1)(b))` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 1 10) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2027 4 10)
-- Case: an application where the section 80 agreement makes the whole benefit payable under the provincial plan.
#ASSERT `Must the Minister forward my application to the authority of a provincial pension plan (reg 43(2))` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Minister forward my application to the authority of a provincial pension plan (reg 43(2))` FALSE FALSE)
-- Case: Ahmed's wife cannot manage her affairs; he holds a power of attorney recognised by law.
#ASSERT `May an application be made on behalf of a person who cannot manage their own affairs (reg 44(1))` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- No one is authorized and the Minister has not approved the applicant.
#ASSERT NOT (`May an application be made on behalf of a person who cannot manage their own affairs (reg 44(1))` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Case: Lena's mother has died; Lena, her child, applies for a division.
#ASSERT `May I apply for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings after a death (reg 44(2))` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I apply for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings after a death (reg 44(2))` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Case: Tom wants to withdraw his 2020 benefit application before payment begins.
#ASSERT `May I withdraw my application for a benefit (reg 45(1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) TRUE TRUE
-- An application made on 28 May 1975 is not within the regulation.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I withdraw my application for a benefit (reg 45(1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1975 5 28) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my withdrawn application for a benefit still be used to decide my eligibility (reg 45(2))` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Can my withdrawn application for a benefit still be used to decide my eligibility (reg 45(2))` FALSE
-- Case: Ingrid got the decision on her division application on 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `What is the last day I may withdraw my application for a division (reg 45(3))` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT `May I withdraw my application for a division (reg 45(3))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I withdraw my application for a division (reg 45(3))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my withdrawn application for a division still be used to decide my eligibility (reg 45(4))` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Can my withdrawn application for a division still be used to decide my eligibility (reg 45(4))` FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I be given written notice that an approved division was withdrawn (reg 45(5))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I be given written notice that an approved division was withdrawn (reg 45(5))` TRUE FALSE)
-- Case: the notice of a division lists items (a), (b) and (c) as applying; the notice has (a) and (b) only.
#ASSERT `Is the notice of the division of my pensionable earnings in the form required (reg 46(2))` TRUE (LIST `seat item 46(2)(a)`, `seat item 46(2)(b)`) (LIST `seat item 46(2)(a)`, `seat item 46(2)(b)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the notice of the division of my pensionable earnings in the form required (reg 46(2))` TRUE (LIST `seat item 46(2)(a)`, `seat item 46(2)(b)`, `seat item 46(2)(c)`) (LIST `seat item 46(2)(a)`, `seat item 46(2)(b)`))
#ASSERT `Which items does the notice of the division still lack (reg 46(2))` (LIST `seat item 46(2)(a)`, `seat item 46(2)(b)`, `seat item 46(2)(c)`) (LIST `seat item 46(2)(a)`) EQUALS (LIST `seat item 46(2)(b)`, `seat item 46(2)(c)`)
#ASSERT `Is the notice that a division was made given as the Regulations require (reg 46(1))` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the notice that a division was made given as the Regulations require (reg 46(1))` FALSE)
#ASSERT `What is the last day on which my division may be cancelled (reg 46(3))` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT `May my division be cancelled (reg 46(3))` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT NOT (`May my division be cancelled (reg 46(3))` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3))
#ASSERT `Is the notice of the assignment in the form required (reg 46.1(2))` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the notice of the assignment in the form required (reg 46.1(2))` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is the notice that an assignment was made given as the Regulations require (reg 46.1(1))` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the notice that an assignment was made given as the Regulations require (reg 46.1(1))` FALSE)

§§ `Cases -- cancelling a benefit (regulation 46.2)`

-- Case: Hana's retirement pension began 15 March 2026; she may ask to cancel until 15 March 2027.
#ASSERT `What is the last day I may ask to cancel my benefit (reg 46.2(1))` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2027 3 15)
#ASSERT `May I still ask the Minister to cancel my benefit (reg 46.2(1))` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 15) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I still ask the Minister to cancel my benefit (reg 46.2(1))` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 16) TRUE)
-- Case: Karim gets a retirement pension (from January 2020) and applies for a disability pension, deemed disabled from December 2019.
#ASSERT `Is my application for a disability pension treated as a request to cancel my retirement pension (reg 46.2(2))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2019 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my application for a disability pension treated as a request to cancel my retirement pension (reg 46.2(2))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 31) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1))
-- Case: a comparable provincial benefit; notice of the decision received 1 February 2026: 90 days gives 2 May 2026.
#ASSERT `What is the last day I may ask to cancel my retirement pension (reg 46.2(2.1))` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 5 2)
#ASSERT `May I ask to cancel my retirement pension because of a comparable provincial decision (reg 46.2(2.1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 5) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 2) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I ask to cancel my retirement pension because of a comparable provincial decision (reg 46.2(2.1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 5) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 3) TRUE)
-- Case: notice of entitlement to the disability pension received 1 February 2026: 60 days gives 2 April 2026.
#ASSERT `What is the last day I may ask to cancel my disability pension (reg 46.2(2.2))` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 4 2)
#ASSERT `May I ask to cancel my disability pension and have my retirement pension reinstated (reg 46.2(2.2))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 2) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I ask to cancel my disability pension and have my retirement pension reinstated (reg 46.2(2.2))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 3) TRUE)
#ASSERT `Must the Minister grant my request to cancel (reg 46.2(3))` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the Minister grant my request to cancel (reg 46.2(3))` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Minister grant my request to cancel (reg 46.2(3))` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Case: the request was granted on 10 March 2026; repay by the end of March 2027.
#ASSERT `What is the last day I must repay after my request to cancel is granted (reg 46.2(4))` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2027 3 31)
#ASSERT `Am I repaying within the time allowed after my request to cancel is granted (reg 46.2(4))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I repaying within the time allowed after my request to cancel is granted (reg 46.2(4))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2027 4 1))

§§ `Cases -- proving my age and identity (regulations 47 to 51)`

-- Case: Elena has a copy of her birth certificate.
#ASSERT `Must my age and identity be determined on a birth certificate or Commission information (reg 47(1))` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my age and identity be determined on a birth certificate or Commission information (reg 47(1))` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister require my original birth certificate (reg 47(2))` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister require my original birth certificate (reg 47(2))` FALSE)
-- Case: Elena's documents were lost in a fire.
#ASSERT `Can the Minister determine my age and identity from other information (reg 47(3))` TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Minister determine my age and identity from Statistics Canada information (reg 47(4))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister determine my age and identity from Statistics Canada information (reg 47(4))` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister accept the determination of my age made elsewhere (reg 49)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister accept the determination of my age made elsewhere (reg 49)` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister make a new determination of my age (reg 50)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister make a new determination of my age (reg 50)` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does the request to Statistics Canada about me meet the prescribed conditions (reg 51(a))` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the request to Statistics Canada about me meet the prescribed conditions (reg 51(a))` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `May the information about me from Statistics Canada be disclosed to this person (reg 51(b))` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the information about me from Statistics Canada be disclosed to this person (reg 51(b))` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Cases -- what I must set out or furnish (regulations 52 to 54.1)`

-- Case: Elena is applying; items (a)(i), (b)(i) and (c) apply; she has given (a)(i).
#ASSERT `Which items must I still set out or furnish for my benefit (reg 52)` TRUE FALSE (LIST `seat item 52(a)(i)`, `seat item 52(b)(i)`, `seat item 52(c)`) (LIST `seat item 52(a)(i)`) EQUALS (LIST `seat item 52(b)(i)`, `seat item 52(c)`)
-- Before the application and without a written request nothing is due yet.
#ASSERT `Which items must I still set out or furnish for my benefit (reg 52)` FALSE FALSE (LIST `seat item 52(a)(i)`) EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Which items must I still set out or furnish about my family allowance months (reg 53)` TRUE FALSE (LIST `seat item 53(a)`, `seat item 53(c)`) (LIST `seat item 53(c)`) EQUALS (LIST `seat item 53(a)`)
#ASSERT `Which items must I still set out or furnish for my application for a division (reg 54(1))` FALSE TRUE (LIST `seat item 54(1) chapeau`, `seat item 54(1)(d)`) EMPTY EQUALS (LIST `seat item 54(1) chapeau`, `seat item 54(1)(d)`)
#ASSERT `Which information relating to my marriage is still lacking (reg 54(2))` (LIST `seat item 54(2)(a)`, `seat item 54(2)(i)`) (LIST `seat item 54(2)(a)`) EQUALS (LIST `seat item 54(2)(i)`)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister require the original of my certificate of marriage (reg 54(3))` TRUE
#ASSERT `Which items must I still set out or furnish for my application for an assignment (reg 54.1(1))` TRUE FALSE (LIST `seat item 54.1(1)(e)`, `seat item 54.1(1)(g)`) (LIST `seat item 54.1(1)(g)`) EQUALS (LIST `seat item 54.1(1)(e)`)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister require the original of my certificate of marriage for an assignment (reg 54.1(2))` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister require the original of my certificate of marriage for an assignment (reg 54.1(2))` FALSE)

§§ `Cases -- when a division takes effect (regulations 54.2 to 54.4)`

-- Case: the marriage information reached the Minister on 15 March 2026: the division takes place 31 March 2026, and the earnings attach from 1 April 2026.
#ASSERT `On what date does the division of my pensionable earnings take place (reg 54.2(1)(a))` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT `On what date is the division of my pensionable earnings approved (reg 54.2(1)(b))` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30)
#ASSERT `From what date are the pensionable earnings attributed to me after a division (reg 54.2(2))` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister act under subsection 58(7) of the Act in my case (reg 54.4)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister act under subsection 58(7) of the Act in my case (reg 54.4)` TRUE FALSE)

§§ `Cases -- payment of my benefit (regulations 55 to 59)`

-- Case: Nadia's father cannot manage his affairs; his guardian, authorized by law, is to be paid his benefit.
#ASSERT `Can the Minister direct that my benefit be paid to someone on my behalf (reg 55(1))` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- The Minister has not found him incapable.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister direct that my benefit be paid to someone on my behalf (reg 55(1))` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `May my benefit be paid to the person or agency the Minister has directed (reg 55(2))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May my benefit be paid to the person or agency the Minister has directed (reg 55(2))` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the person or agency paid my benefit on my behalf account to the Minister (reg 55(3))` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the person or agency paid my benefit on my behalf account to the Minister (reg 55(3))` FALSE)
-- Case: Paul's benefit is $1.99 a month and he gets no Old Age Security pension.
#ASSERT `Can the Minister pay my small benefit in arrears at intervals (reg 56)` 1.99 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister pay my small benefit in arrears at intervals (reg 56)` 2 FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is the interval at which my small benefit is paid no longer than yearly (reg 56)` 12
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the interval at which my small benefit is paid no longer than yearly (reg 56)` 13)
-- Case: Rita died owed a payment; there is an estate. Another died with no estate: the Minister's designate. Another is owed nothing.
#ASSERT `Who may be paid a benefit payment unpaid at the beneficiary's death (reg 57)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the estate of the deceased beneficiary`
#ASSERT `Who may be paid a benefit payment unpaid at the beneficiary's death (reg 57)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a person or agency designated by the Minister`
#ASSERT `Who may be paid a benefit payment unpaid at the beneficiary's death (reg 57)` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `nobody under regulation 57`
-- Case: Henri was paid a benefit by the Government of Canada in December 1974 for Plan and Quebec Pension Plan contributions.
#ASSERT `Can the Minister direct that my benefit be paid as a single monthly payment (reg 58(1))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister direct that my benefit be paid as a single monthly payment (reg 58(1))` TRUE FALSE)
-- Case: written notice of withholding given 1 January 2026: withholding may start 31 January 2026.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest day the Minister may start to withhold my benefit (reg 59(1))` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister withhold my benefit from a given day (reg 59(1))` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister withhold my benefit from a given day (reg 59(1))` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 30))
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Minister keep withholding my benefit (reg 59(1))` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `May the Minister keep withholding my benefit (reg 59(1))` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I paid for a day of the period my benefit was withheld (reg 59(2))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I paid for a day of the period my benefit was withheld (reg 59(2))` TRUE FALSE)

§§ `Cases -- applying for a retirement pension, and the annual adjustment (regulations 61 and 62)`

#ASSERT `For which years must I file a statement of my contributory earnings (reg 61)` 2026 FALSE EQUALS (LIST 2026)
#ASSERT `For which years must I file a statement of my contributory earnings (reg 61)` 2026 TRUE EQUALS (LIST 2026, 2025)
-- Case: a benefit of $800.00 before adjustment and a ratio of 1.0235 (expressed as 1.024): 819.20.
#ASSERT `What is my basic monthly benefit after the annual adjustment (reg 62)` 800 1.0235 EQUALS 819.2
-- 725.37 x 1.024 = 742.77888: cents round to 742.78.
#ASSERT `What is my basic monthly benefit after the annual adjustment (reg 62)` 725.37 1.0235 EQUALS 742.78

§§ `Cases -- proving a relationship or a death (regulation 63)`

#ASSERT `Must the Minister use the information in paragraphs (a) to (c) to decide a relationship or a death (reg 63(1))` TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I furnish this certificate or copy to the Minister (reg 63(2))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I furnish this certificate or copy to the Minister (reg 63(2))` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister require the original of the document I furnished (reg 63(3))` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister require the original of the document I furnished (reg 63(3))` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must I furnish other information or evidence about my relationship to the person (reg 63(4))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I furnish other information or evidence about my relationship to the person (reg 63(4))` FALSE TRUE)

§§ `Cases -- the death benefit when the estate does not claim it (regulation 64)`

-- Case: a contributor died 1 January 2020 and the estate has not applied for the death benefit.
#ASSERT `Can a direction be given to pay the death benefit to someone other than the estate (reg 64(1))` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) 5000 60000
-- The estate applied on 1 March 2020, the 60th day after the death: in time, and no amount test applies after 2018.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a direction be given to pay the death benefit to someone other than the estate (reg 64(1))` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1) 5000 60000)
#ASSERT `Can a direction be given to pay the death benefit to someone other than the estate (reg 64(1))` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 2) 5000 60000
-- A death in June 2010 with a death benefit of 2,000 (under $2,387) and an estate that applied in time.
#ASSERT `Can a direction be given to pay the death benefit to someone other than the estate (reg 64(1))` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2010 6 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 6 10) 2000 46300
#ASSERT `Who is paid the death benefit when the estate does not claim it (reg 64(1))` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the individual or institution that paid or is responsible for the payment of the funeral expenses`
#ASSERT `Who is paid the death benefit when the estate does not claim it (reg 64(1))` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the survivor of the deceased contributor`
#ASSERT `Who is paid the death benefit when the estate does not claim it (reg 64(1))` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nobody under regulation 64`
-- Case: funeral expenses 1,800 and a death benefit of 2,500: 1,800 to the funeral payer and 700 remains.
#ASSERT `How much of the death benefit may be paid to the person who paid the funeral expenses (reg 64(2))` 1800 2500 EQUALS 1800
#ASSERT `How much of the death benefit remains to be directed (reg 64(3))` 1800 2500 EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `Who is paid the remainder of the death benefit (reg 64(3))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the survivor of the deceased contributor`
#ASSERT `Who is paid the remainder of the death benefit (reg 64(3))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the next of kin of the deceased contributor`

§§ `Cases -- children and school (regulations 65 to 67)`

-- Case: Alma, a survivor, provides 600 of the 1,000 provided for the children.
#ASSERT `Do I maintain the deceased contributor's dependent children wholly or substantially (reg 65)` 600 1000
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I maintain the deceased contributor's dependent children wholly or substantially (reg 65)` 500 1000)
#ASSERT `Do I maintain the child of a deceased contributor (reg 65.1(a))` TRUE 100 100
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I maintain the child of a deceased contributor (reg 65.1(a))` TRUE 99.99 100)
#ASSERT `Do I maintain the child of a disabled contributor (reg 65.1(b))` TRUE 100 100
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I maintain the child of a disabled contributor (reg 65.1(b))` FALSE 250 100)
-- Case: a 19-year-old attends university and is enrolled in what the university calls a full-time load.
#ASSERT `Is the child in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university (reg 66(1))` TRUE TRUE 1 EQUALS `full-time attendance at a school or university`
#ASSERT `Is the child in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university (reg 66(1))` TRUE FALSE 0.2 EQUALS `part-time attendance at a school or university`
#ASSERT `Is the child in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university (reg 66(1))` TRUE FALSE 0.19 EQUALS `no attendance at a school or university`
#ASSERT `Is the child considered to be in attendance during a school vacation (reg 66(2))` `full-time attendance at a school or university` `the child is absent during a normal period of scholastic vacation`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the child considered to be in attendance during a school vacation (reg 66(2))` `full-time attendance at a school or university` `the child is not absent`)
#ASSERT `Is the child absent because of illness considered to be in attendance (reg 66(3))` `full-time attendance at a school or university` `the child is absent because of illness` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the child absent because of illness considered to be in attendance (reg 66(3))` `full-time attendance at a school or university` `the child is absent because of illness` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is the child considered to be in attendance on this day (reg 66(4))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 8 31) (YearMonthDay 2026 8 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the child considered to be in attendance on this day (reg 66(4))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 8 31) (YearMonthDay 2026 9 1))
#ASSERT `Until when is the child considered to have been in attendance (reg 66(5))` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT `Must I file an attestation signed by my child that the child attended school (reg 67)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I file an attestation signed by my child that the child attended school (reg 67)` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does what I filed about my child's attendance meet the Regulations (reg 67)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does what I filed about my child's attendance meet the Regulations (reg 67)` TRUE FALSE)

§§ `Cases -- a disability pension (regulations 68 to 72)`

`seat item 68(1)(a)(i)` MEANS `reg 68(1)(a)(i) — a report of the nature, extent and prognosis of the disability`
`seat item 68(1)(a)(ii)` MEANS `reg 68(1)(a)(ii) — a report of the findings upon which the diagnosis and prognosis were made`
`seat item 68(1)(a)(iii)` MEANS `reg 68(1)(a)(iii) — a report of any limitation resulting from the disability`
`seat item 68(1)(a)(iv)` MEANS `reg 68(1)(a)(iv) — a report of any other pertinent information, including recommendations for further diagnostic work or treatment`
`seat item 68(1)(b)` MEANS `reg 68(1)(b) — a statement of the person's occupation and earnings for the period commencing on the date the applicant alleges the disability commenced`
`seat item 68(1)(c)` MEANS `reg 68(1)(c) — a statement of the person's education, employment experience and activities of daily life`
`seat item 72(2)(a)` MEANS `reg 72(2)(a) — the applicant's name, address and Social Insurance Number and, if applicable, the name and address of the person making the request for the applicant and that person's relationship to the applicant`
`seat item 72(2)(b)` MEANS `reg 72(2)(b) — the month in which the applicant ceased to receive the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit`
`seat item 72(2)(c)` MEANS `reg 72(2)(c) — the month in which the applicant became incapable again of working`
`seat item 72(2)(d)` MEANS `reg 72(2)(d) — the date that the applicant stopped working`
`seat item 72(2)(e)` MEANS `reg 72(2)(e) — the statement of a person qualified to practise medicine confirming a severe and prolonged disability that is the same as, or related to, the disability that entitled the applicant to the pension or benefit`
`seat item 72(2)(f)` MEANS `reg 72(2)(f) — the name of each dependent child of the applicant and whether the applicant has at least 20% of the parenting time in respect of the child`
`seat item 72(2)(g)(i)` MEANS `reg 72(2)(g)(i) — for each child aged 18 or more whose disabled contributor's child benefit is to be reinstated, the child's name, address and Social Insurance Number`
`seat item 72(2)(g)(ii)` MEANS `reg 72(2)(g)(ii) — for each such child, evidence, established in accordance with section 67, of full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university`
`seat item 74.1(1)(a)` MEANS `reg 74.1(1)(a) — the name, address and Social Insurance Number of the contributor`
`seat item 74.1(1)(b)` MEANS `reg 74.1(1)(b) — where the person making the request is not the contributor, that person's name and address and relationship to the contributor`
`seat item 74.1(1)(c)` MEANS `reg 74.1(1)(c) — the grounds for the request and a statement of the facts that form the basis of it`

-- Case: Vikram claims a disability and has supplied the nature report (a)(i) and the statement of occupation (b).
#ASSERT `Which items must I still supply about the disability I claim (reg 68(1))` TRUE (LIST `seat item 68(1)(a)(i)`, `seat item 68(1)(b)`) EQUALS (LIST `seat item 68(1)(a)(ii)`, `seat item 68(1)(a)(iii)`, `seat item 68(1)(a)(iv)`, `seat item 68(1)(c)`)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister require me to supply a statement of my occupation and earnings (reg 68(2)(a))` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister require me to supply a statement of my occupation and earnings (reg 68(2)(a))` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister require me to undergo special examinations and supply reports (reg 68(2)(b))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister require me to undergo special examinations and supply reports (reg 68(2)(b))` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Will the reasonable cost of an examination or report the Minister required be reimbursed to me (reg 68(3))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Will the reasonable cost of an examination or report the Minister required be reimbursed to me (reg 68(3))` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is this travel or living expense part of the cost of my examination (reg 68(4))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this travel or living expense part of the cost of my examination (reg 68(4))` TRUE FALSE)
-- Case: Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average 60,000 and a monthly flat rate benefit of 600: (15,000 x .75) + 7,200 = 18,450.
#ASSERT `What is the maximum annual amount a person could receive as a disability pension (reg 68.1(1))` 60000 600 EQUALS 18450
#ASSERT `Is my work substantially gainful (reg 68.1(1))` 18450 60000 600
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my work substantially gainful (reg 68.1(1))` 18449.99 60000 600)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister require me to undergo examinations and supply reports and statements (reg 69(1))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister require me to undergo examinations and supply reports and statements (reg 69(1))` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister require me to undergo rehabilitation measures (reg 69(2))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister require me to undergo rehabilitation measures (reg 69(2))` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Will the reasonable cost of a measure the Minister required be reimbursed to me (reg 69(3))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Will the reasonable cost of a measure the Minister required be reimbursed to me (reg 69(3))` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is this travel or living expense part of the cost of a measure the Minister required (reg 69(4))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this travel or living expense part of the cost of a measure the Minister required (reg 69(4))` TRUE FALSE)
-- Case: Vikram skipped a medical examination the Minister required, with no risk to his health.
#ASSERT `Can I be determined to have ceased to be disabled because I did not comply (reg 70(1))` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Had the examination been a significant risk to his life or health, there would be good cause.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be determined to have ceased to be disabled because I did not comply (reg 70(1))` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is my failure to comply for good cause (reg 70(2))` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my failure to comply for good cause (reg 70(2))` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is the time I am determined to have ceased to be disabled not earlier than the day I failed to comply (reg 70(1))` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the time I am determined to have ceased to be disabled not earlier than the day I failed to comply (reg 70(1))` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28))
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Minister that I have returned to work (reg 70.1)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I tell the Minister that I have returned to work (reg 70.1)` TRUE FALSE)
-- Case: Vikram became incapable again in March 2026.
#ASSERT `Is my request for reinstatement made as the Regulations require (reg 71(1))` TRUE
#ASSERT `What is the last day I may ask to have my disability pension reinstated (reg 71(2))` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2027 3 31)
#ASSERT `Is my request for reinstatement of my disability pension in time (reg 71(2))` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my request for reinstatement of my disability pension in time (reg 71(2))` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 4 1))
#ASSERT `Must the Minister decide on the information and evidence I furnished (reg 72(1))` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Minister decide on the information and evidence I furnished (reg 72(1))` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Which items must I still furnish with my request for reinstatement (reg 72(2))` FALSE (LIST `seat item 72(2)(a)`, `seat item 72(2)(c)`) EQUALS (LIST `seat item 72(2)(b)`, `seat item 72(2)(d)`, `seat item 72(2)(e)`, `seat item 72(2)(f)`)
#ASSERT `Which items must I still furnish with my request for reinstatement (reg 72(2))` TRUE (LIST `seat item 72(2)(a)`, `seat item 72(2)(b)`, `seat item 72(2)(c)`, `seat item 72(2)(d)`, `seat item 72(2)(e)`, `seat item 72(2)(f)`) EQUALS (LIST `seat item 72(2)(g)(i)`, `seat item 72(2)(g)(ii)`)

§§ `Cases -- reconsideration and appeal (regulations 74 to 74.2)`

#ASSERT `May someone make a request for reconsideration or an appeal for me (reg 74)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May someone make a request for reconsideration or an appeal for me (reg 74)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Which items must my request for reconsideration still set out (reg 74.1(1))` TRUE (LIST `seat item 74.1(1)(a)`) EQUALS (LIST `seat item 74.1(1)(b)`, `seat item 74.1(1)(c)`)
#ASSERT `Which items must my request for reconsideration still set out (reg 74.1(1))` FALSE (LIST `seat item 74.1(1)(a)`) EQUALS (LIST `seat item 74.1(1)(c)`)
#ASSERT `Is my request for reconsideration made as the Regulations require (reg 74.1(1))` TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Minister take steps to obtain information that my request left out (reg 74.1(2))` TRUE
-- Case: notified 1 January 2026; the 365-day period ends 1 January 2027; a request on 2 January 2027 needs the further tests.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of the 365-day period after I was notified (reg 74.1(4)(a))` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `May the Minister allow me a longer period to ask for a reconsideration (reg 74.1(3) and (4))` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 2) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Minister allow me a longer period to ask for a reconsideration (reg 74.1(3) and (4))` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 2) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- A request within the 365 days needs only the explanation and the continuing intention.
#ASSERT `May the Minister allow me a longer period to ask for a reconsideration (reg 74.1(3) and (4))` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the notification of my appealable decision given as the Regulations require (reg 74.2)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the notification of my appealable decision given as the Regulations require (reg 74.2)` TRUE FALSE)

§§ `Cases -- the Pension Index (regulation 75)`

-- Case: monthly Consumer Price Index figures 100 to 111: 1,266 / 12 = 105.5.
#ASSERT `What is the Pension Index for the year (reg 75)` (LIST 100, 101, 102, 103, 104, 105, 106, 107, 108, 109, 110, 111) EQUALS JUST 105.5
#ASSERT `What is the Pension Index for the year (reg 75)` (LIST 100, 101, 102, 103, 104, 105, 106, 107, 108, 109, 110) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Cases -- deductions from my benefit, and family allowance months (regulations 76 to 77)`

-- Case: Dora's province advanced her welfare; she signed an irrevocable consent on 1 March 2025; the excess payment is 500.
#ASSERT `How much may be deducted from my lump sum and paid to the authority (reg 76(2))` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) 500 FALSE EQUALS JUST 500
-- A deduction has already been authorized for this excess payment: no other amount.
#ASSERT `How much may be deducted from my lump sum and paid to the authority (reg 76(2))` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) 500 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An excess payment of exactly $50 is not "greater than $50".
#ASSERT `How much may be deducted from my lump sum and paid to the authority (reg 76(2))` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) 50 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the Minister deduct an amount from my benefit and pay it to the administrator (reg 76.1(1))` `a disability pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) 50.01
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister deduct an amount from my benefit and pay it to the administrator (reg 76.1(1))` `a retirement pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1) 1000)
-- Case: Greta stayed home with her child born 15 June 2015 until 30 June 2022; the child reached seven on 1 July 2022 (section 2(2)).
#ASSERT `Am I a family allowance recipient for the purposes of the Act (reg 77)` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 6 30) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a family allowance recipient for the purposes of the Act (reg 77)` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Cases -- which months count as months of cohabitation (regulations 78 to 78.2)`

-- Case: Eli and Fay separated for 91 days; neither for work nor illness.
#ASSERT `Does this separation interrupt our cohabitation (reg 78(2))` 91 FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this separation interrupt our cohabitation (reg 78(2))` 90 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `From what day is our cohabitation deemed to have ceased (reg 78(3))` 2019 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2019 1 1)
-- Case: a month in March 2018, before the interruption that began in 2019: counts. A month in March 2019 does not, unless it precedes the 36-month minimum.
#ASSERT `Is this a month during which we have cohabited (reg 78(1))` (YearMonthDay 2018 3 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE 2019 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this a month during which we have cohabited (reg 78(1))` (YearMonthDay 2019 3 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE 2019 FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is this a month during which we have cohabited (reg 78(1))` (YearMonthDay 2019 3 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE 2019 TRUE
-- Case: married 15 June 2010; commenced to live apart 10 March 2013 and resumed 1 February 2015; divorced 20 September 2018.
#ASSERT `Is this a month during which we cohabited for the division of pensionable earnings (reg 78.1(1))` (YearMonthDay 2012 6 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2013 3 10), (YearMonthDay 2018 9 20)) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2013 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2015 2 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this a month during which we cohabited for the division of pensionable earnings (reg 78.1(1))` (YearMonthDay 2014 6 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2013 3 10), (YearMonthDay 2018 9 20)) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2013 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2015 2 1))
#ASSERT `Have we cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year (reg 78.1(2))` (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2011 6 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`Have we cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year (reg 78.1(2))` (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2011 5 10))
#ASSERT `Does our separation by reason of work or illness not interrupt our cohabitation (reg 78.1(3))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our separation by reason of work or illness not interrupt our cohabitation (reg 78.1(3))` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is this month in our period of cohabitation (reg 78.2)` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this month in our period of cohabitation (reg 78.2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Cases -- taking my retirement pension early or late (regulations 78.3 and 78.4)`

-- Case: Maya, born 15 March 1960, starts her pension in January 2024: 15 months before April 2025 at 0.60% a month: 1 - 0.09.
#ASSERT `By what factor is my retirement pension reduced because it starts before 65 (reg 78.3)` (YearMonthDay 1960 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.91
-- A start before 2011 is not covered by the text.
#ASSERT `By what factor is my retirement pension reduced because it starts before 65 (reg 78.3)` (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2010 12 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Case: Noor, born 15 March 1955, starts her pension in January 2023: 33 months after April 2020 at 0.70% a month: 1 + 0.231.
#ASSERT `By what factor is my retirement pension increased because it starts after 65 (reg 78.4)` (YearMonthDay 1955 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2023 1 1) EQUALS JUST 1.231
#ASSERT `By what factor is my retirement pension increased because it starts after 65 (reg 78.4)` (YearMonthDay 1955 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) EQUALS NOTHING
